{"agent_id":"pp3g-Yc8o-fix-the-orchestrator-git-merge-hard-block-regression","agent_seq":5,"timestamp":"2026-08-06T04:15:29.487467658Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"7efd07df-fbdf-492d-a2cc-7754eb5448b4","comment_uuid":"aa2fe785-4cf6-4bf4-a156-f33fcc0b70c3","author":"pp3g-Yc8o-fix-the-orchestrator-git-merge-hard-block-regression","content":"Result: #204 FIXED and VERIFIED LIVE. Commit 48011ba (2 files, .opencode/plugins/crosslink-guard.ts + orchestrator-guard.ts).\n\n## ROOT CAUSE (corrects the issue hypothesis)\nThe issue hypothesized 'chat.params is not firing'. Evidence disproves that — chat.params IS firing; the a73d12f fix is flawed because it stored the runtime agent in ONE module-level variable (runtimeAgentFromChat) shared across ALL sessions in an opencode process. One process hosts the interactive session plus Task-tool subagents, and every session's chat.params fires in that same process. Proven from logs: run 36f6bb28 processed subagent ses_02ae84e70 (agent=reviewer) at 03:24:11.551; reviewer chat.params at 03:24:11.553 overwrote the shared variable; the orchestrator's merge (call_00_ET_z6d1b2...) intercepted at 03:24:15.068 resolved to 'reviewer' and by_type.reviewer BLOCKED git merge at 03:24:15.080 (MANDATORY COMPLIANCE). Plugin load order is NOT the cause (fork source plugin/index.ts trigger() iterates ALL registered hooks; both plugins receive chat.params).\n\n## FIX (per-session agent resolution)\n1. crosslink-guard.ts: replaced single runtimeAgentFromChat with runtimeAgentBySession Map<sessionID, {agent, source}>. chat.params AND new chat.message hook both capture per-session agent (redundancy covers variants where chat.params may not fire). applyAgentTypeOverride is now session-aware: session agent (1st) > CROSSLINK_AGENT_TYPE env (2nd) > hook-config agent.type (3rd); source attribution preserved in logs.\n2. orchestrator-guard.ts: same per-session Map; tool.execute.before resolves agent for THIS session only, with NO cross-session fallback when sessionID present (prevents a builder subagent event from authorizing an orchestrator write).\n\n## LIVE VERIFICATION (fresh orchestrator process, post-restart scenario)\nLaunched 'opencode run --model opencode-go/deepseek-v4-flash --agent orchestrator' in this worktree (fresh plugin load from fixed disk files) against scratch branches test/204-merge-base + test/204-merge-topic. Guard log at 04:10:15:\n- 'chat.params agent: orchestrator session: ses_02abd3de5ffelQtWCYvt77Klyd' (new per-session format)\n- 'by_type override applied for agent: orchestrator (source: chat.params)'\n- 'ALLOW: gated git, active issue sentinel present: 204'\n- 'ALLOW: gated git with active issue: git merge --ff-only test/204-merge-topic'\n- Merge FAST-FORWARDED 0142980..bac6081, exit 0 — NOT root-blocked.\nClobber-proof evidence: a 'chat.params agent: build' event from a different session fired at 04:10:14.905, 0.3s before the merge, yet the orchestrator session still resolved as orchestrator at 04:10:15.210 — the per-session map prevents the cross-session clobber that caused the regression.\n\n## VALIDATION\n- bun build (the actual plugin runtime) both files: clean.\n- tsc: only pre-existing @types/node noise (fs/path/os/process TS2307/TS2580 — same as noted in #173 review); zero errors in the changed regions.\n\n## LEFTOVERS\n- Scratch branches test/204-merge-base (now at bac6081 post-merge) + test/204-merge-topic left as evidence; branch deletion blocked for builder. Operator can: git branch -D test/204-merge-base test/204-merge-topic\n- No push. No issue close. Existing interactive orchestrator TUI processes still run the OLD plugin module (loaded at process start) — operator restart required to pick up 48011ba; after restart, orchestrator merge will be gated correctly in-process.\n- .crosslink/.last-hydrated-ref churn + .kickoff-session untracked (pre-existing, not committed).","created_at":"2026-08-06T04:15:29.458114152Z","kind":"result","signed_by":"SHA256:H5ghTa8b3msD